From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@zoho.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:26:32 +0300
Subject: Load .spm meshes on big-endian hosts

The SPM loader refused to run on big-endian machines ("Not little endian
machine"), so no kart, track or model loaded. The files are little-endian:
read every multi-byte field (header bounding box, counts, positions, packed
normals and tangents, half-float UVs and weights, joint indices, indices,
armature joints, parent infos, frames and their loc/rot/scale floats)
through GE::readLE, which byte-swaps after the read on big-endian hosts and
does nothing on little-endian ones.

The armature reader also read 1- and 2-byte fields into 4-byte unsigned
variables, which only gives the right value on little-endian hosts; they
are read into variables of the stored width now.

